; An (executable), NOT a (test): deliberately OUT of the `runtest` alias.
;
; Measured on CI, this one binary was 652s of the Test step's 756s -- the
; single dominant cost of `dune runtest`, and by extension of the whole
; workflow's critical path. Its QCheck property groups (not the oracle group,
; which skips under runtest since MARCH_BIN is unset and the compiler exe
; isn't findable from the test's cwd) run generated programs through the full
; parse -> typecheck -> lower -> mono -> defun -> perceus pipeline hundreds of
; times each, and alcotest has no parallelism whatsoever -- it runs cases
; sequentially in-process, with no --jobs/--parallel of any kind -- so the
; only way to shorten it is to run several filtered processes concurrently.
;
; .github/workflows/ci.yml therefore runs it as its own parallel job(s), which
; also keeps the two halves of this binary from fighting over one timeout: the
; `property-tests` job runs the property groups, while `property-oracle` runs
; the interp-vs-compiled oracle group (8 shards, MARCH_BIN set).
;
; It is still BUILT by CI (the ocaml-build job builds test/test_properties.exe
; and fans it out), so a compile error here still fails the build -- just not
; via `dune runtest`. Run the whole thing locally with:
;   dune build @test/property_tests
(executable
 (name test_properties)
 (modules test_properties)
 (libraries march_lexer march_parser march_ast march_desugar march_typecheck march_errors march_eval march_tir march_scheduler march_modules alcotest qcheck-core qcheck-alcotest))

(rule
 (alias property_tests)
 (action (run %{exe:test_properties.exe})))

