; ── Capability mocking as a user writes it: inside a `test` block ─────────
; Companion to cap_mock_io above, which drives `main` and diffs stdout. This
; one uses the real API surface -- a `test` block, `root_cap` attenuated to the
; capability, assertions doing the checking -- because that is how anyone would
; actually reach for this, and it is a different path through the elaboration
; (a test entry point is a ROOT: its arity is frozen because the test runner
; calls it, so the capability arrives through `with_cap` rather than through a
; threaded parameter).
;
; The fixture asserts the unmocked clock on BOTH sides of `with_cap`, so it
; cannot pass if `unix_time_ms` merely returned the mocked value always.
(rule
 (targets cap_mock_clock_bin cap_mock_clock.out)
 (deps (file %{exe:../bin/main.exe})
       (file ../runtime/march_runtime.c) (file ../runtime/march_runtime.h)
       (file ../runtime/march_scheduler.c) (file ../runtime/march_scheduler.h)
       (file ../runtime/march_heap.c) (file ../runtime/march_heap.h)
