; ── Regression: Actor.call replies must be correlation-checked ──
; A first call times out (its handler replies late); the caller then issues a
; second call. Without correlating the reply to the call that's actually
; waiting, the stale first reply is delivered as the second call's answer.
; This fixture burns time in the handler so the first call's 1ms deadline
; expires before the reply lands, then makes a second call and checks it
; gets the SECOND reply (n=1), not the stale first one (n=0). Needs the real
; stdlib (List.fold_left, Range), hence (source_tree ../stdlib). Compile
; natively, run, diff.
