; ── Regression: burst-of-task_spawn must not race the Task object ──
; march_task_spawn_thunk initialised the Task's proc-handle/result/done-flag
; AFTER march_sched_spawn published the proc, so a work-stealing scheduler
; thread could run the thunk trampoline (which writes the result and
; release-stores the done flag) before the spawner returned — the spawner then
; clobbered the completed result/done flag back to zero (TSan-confirmed race
; at march_runtime.c:1833 vs the post-spawn store; symptom: task_await hangs or
; returns a zeroed result).  This program spawns a burst of tasks up front,
; then awaits them all and checks the exact sum, repeated over many rounds so
; the non-deterministic race is likely to fire.  Compile natively, run, diff.
; To also catch it under a race detector: compile with MARCH_SANITIZE=thread
; and run ~100x — expect no ThreadSanitizer report.
(rule
 (targets native_task_burst_await native_task_burst_await.out)
 (deps (file %{exe:../bin/main.exe})
