; ── Erased/uniform boundary between the C runtime and compiled code ──────
; One family, three fixtures.  march_vault_get / march_record_get / the vault
; key builtins all hand a value across a boundary where the runtime has ONE
; fixed representation and the compiled call site decodes by the STATIC type;
; every bug below is those two disagreeing.  All were compiled-only, with the
; interpreter correct, and all three .march files carry their own mechanism
; write-up plus a note on why the EVEN-Int cases are not redundant.
;
;   vault_niche_unsafe_element   runtime returns the NICHE Option encoding
;                                unconditionally; the call site decodes BOXED
;                                for a niche-unsafe element (nested Option,
;                                Float, Unit) -> non-exhaustive panic / SIGSEGV
;   record_erased_field_repr     a Float field handed back as raw IEEE-754 bits
;                                where an erased consumer needs a
;                                march_alloc_float box, plus the boxed
;                                Option(Float) cell that llvm_case unboxes ->
;                                SIGSEGV in march_unbox_float /
;                                march_string_concat3
;   vault_non_string_key         a non-String key: fixed by PR #315 without a
;                                fixture, pinned here
;   record_get_let_bound_eq      an un-annotated `let` LET-GENERALIZED the
;                                record_get result, so the call site emitted the
;                                erased kind 'g' while the other operand of `==`
;                                was a boxed Option(Float) -> silently `false`
;
; These use stdlib modules (Vault, List) and link the C runtime, so they need
; BOTH source trees staged plus MARCH_RUNTIME_DIR — without them the compile
; silently picks up a stale tree.
(rule
 (targets native_vault_niche_unsafe_element native_vault_niche_unsafe_element.out)
