; QUARANTINED from `runtest` (2026-07-24): reddened `test (ubuntu-24.04)`
; on a signal-dispatch ordering/content race. Not a simple line-ordering
; flake — reproduced locally at ~2-5% of runs (looping the compiled binary
; hundreds to thousands of times), and the majority shape is TORN output
; (e.g. `survived termterm handler` — a dropped newline / concatenated
; lines), not a clean 3-line permutation a sorted diff could tolerate (that
; was only ~1 in 5 of the failures; the rest genuinely corrupt content, so
; `node_discovery`'s sort-before-diff approach above does not apply here).
; Ruled out march_println/march_print's unchecked writev(2)/write(2) return
; value (the scheduler's SIGUSR1 preemption tick can EINTR a syscall — see
; march_scheduler.c's "Limitations / known EINTR exposure") as the cause: a
; retry-on-short-write fix was implemented and tested, but a guaranteed-fresh
; compile (MARCH_NO_RUNTIME_CACHE=1, caches cleared) with that fix still
; flaked at the same ~5% rate, so the corruption happens before the write
; syscall — most likely a race between the deferred Signal.watch dispatch
; (run by an arbitrary scheduler OS thread's per-iteration drain, per
; march_scheduler.c's march_signal_drain call sites) and the raising
; thread's own subsequent code, touching overlapping memory (allocator/GC)
; rather than just interleaving output. Same general class as the open
; scheduler-deadlock P0 in specs/todos.md (heisenbug: not yet isolated to
; an exact missing sync edge) but a distinct symptom — tracked as a
; separate entry there. Un-quarantine (restore `(alias runtest)` below)
; once the dispatch race is fixed. Runnable manually via
; `dune build @test/signal_term_suppress_quarantined`.  Full quarantine
; inventory (what coverage this leaves dark): specs/todos.md.
(rule
 (alias signal_term_suppress_quarantined)
 (action (diff native/signal_term_suppress.expected native_signal_term_suppress.out)))

; ── Phase 2: float-boxing Stage 2 (erased Floats are heap-boxed) ──────
; A Float crossing a type-erasure boundary is boxed (march_float_box, tag -3),
; so RC on the erased slot is sound and generic compare dispatches on the box
; tag.  Exercises List.map+named-fn (clo_wrap ptr ABI), Ok(Float) round-trip,
; and the erased-Float lambda comparator through mergesort_by (the original P0
; that SIGSEGV'd / mis-sorted compiled).  (source_tree ../stdlib) for Sort/List.
(rule
 (targets native_float_boxing native_float_boxing.out)
 (deps (file %{exe:../bin/main.exe})
       (file ../runtime/march_runtime.c) (file ../runtime/march_runtime.h)
       (file ../runtime/march_scheduler.c) (file ../runtime/march_scheduler.h)
