; ── Witness: DOUBLE-collision (shared ctor name) GENERAL-interface dispatch ──
; Constructor module-qualified identity plan flag-day
; (specs/plans/2026-07-20-fqn-impl-dispatch-identity.md, Task 6): the sibling of
; speak_collision_native above, but the two same-short-name `Thing` types ALSO
; share a constructor NAME (`Shared`) — a "double collision". This shape was
; rejected by the interim Task-6b coherence stopgap because the backends used to
; route dispatch on the BARE ctor tag (ci_module diagnostic-only), so `speak`
; would misdispatch. The plan qualifies each colliding type's ctor identity with
; its declaring module in native ECon/pattern-match (and the interpreter's VCon
; tag), so `speak(Shared)` routes to the correct module's impl body. The fixture
; compiles natively and RUNS the binary, which panics (exit 1) on any misdispatch
; (`from-A`/`from-B` must each reach their own impl body). The entry asserts BOTH
; directions at once, so it catches order-dependent misdispatch regardless of the
; file-walk order (see dc_entry.march). Run interpreted too, manually.
(rule
 (alias runtest)
 (deps (file %{exe:../bin/main.exe})
       (file ../runtime/march_runtime.c) (file ../runtime/march_runtime.h)
