; ── Regression: a Float-returning Task must work compiled.  Two defects made
; ── EVERY Float task unusable natively while the interpreter was correct:
; ── (1) task_await's "double" arm unboxed the march_float_box in the Ok
; ── payload and stored raw double bits back, so the Ok(v) destructure unboxed
; ── a SECOND time and dereferenced the IEEE-754 pattern -> SIGSEGV, no output;
; ── (2) a zero-arg lambda's closure temp was typed from its span (the RETURN
; ── type, not `() -> ret`), so Task.async's captured thunk emitted `load
; ── double` for a closure ptr and clang rejected the module outright.
; ── This leg covers the documented stdlib surface (async / await /
; ── await_unwrap / await_many / async_stream) and needs BOTH fixes; the
; ── task_spawn_float_thunk leg below isolates (1).  There was no Float task
; ── coverage at all before these, which is why both shipped.  Floats print as
; ── scaled Ints so the golden does not depend on float_to_string.  Run
; ── single-threaded so the sequential await prints serialise; diff stdout.
(rule
 (targets native_task_await_float native_task_await_float.out)
 (deps (file %{exe:../bin/main.exe})
       (file ../runtime/march_runtime.c) (file ../runtime/march_runtime.h)
       (file ../runtime/march_scheduler.c) (file ../runtime/march_scheduler.h)
       (file ../runtime/march_heap.c) (file ../runtime/march_heap.h)
       (file ../runtime/march_gc.c) (file ../runtime/march_gc.h)
       (file ../runtime/march_message.c) (file ../runtime/march_message.h)
       (file ../runtime/march_deque.h)
       (file ../runtime/march_extras.c) (file ../runtime/march_ctx_escape.c) (file ../runtime/march_compress.c)
       (file ../runtime/base64.c) (file ../runtime/sha1.c)
       (file native/task_await_float.march))
 (action
  (progn
   (run %{exe:../bin/main.exe} --compile -o native_task_await_float
        native/task_await_float.march)
   (with-stdout-to native_task_await_float.out
        (system "MARCH_NUM_SCHEDULERS=1 ./native_task_await_float")))))

