; fold_u8 didn't exist at all. Every case uses a NON-COMMUTATIVE fold so the
; (init, arr, f) vs. march_typed_array_fold's (arr, acc, f) vs. the stdlib
; wrapper's (arr, acc, f) argument-order landmine can't hide behind a
; commutative operator. Also proves the accumulator crosses the closure
; boundary correctly in its erased/boxed representation via the trailing
; fold-into-a-List case.
(rule
