; Task 4b: SIMD vector values crossing march-internal CALL boundaries.
;
; Correctness half (defect A): `nested_dot` is a locally-defined recursive
; `fn` capturing its arrays and threading the vector accumulator as a
; parameter. defun lifts it to a `go$apply$N` closure wrapper reached by two
; call sites -- the direct kickoff call and the closure's own indirect
; self-call -- which must agree on ONE convention for the vector param.
; They did not: the indirect site boxed (uniform ptr closure ABI) while the
; direct site passed the raw <4 x float> register, so the callee dereferenced
; a register vector as a box pointer and segfaulted (exit 139) at every --opt
; level while the interpreter printed the right answer. .expected is
; interpreter-produced; compiled must match byte-for-byte.
(rule
 (targets simd_nested_closure_acc simd_nested_closure_acc.out)
 (deps (file %{exe:../bin/main.exe})
       (glob_files ../runtime/*.c) (glob_files ../runtime/*.h)
