; ── Previously-unwired test/stdlib/*.march describe/test corpus ──────────
; 37 of the 94 files in test/stdlib/ had real, substantial describe/test
; coverage (237 describe blocks) but ran under NO automated runner -- only
; manually, via `march test test/stdlib/<f>.march`. See
; specs/progress/2026-08-11-test-stdlib-march-files-not-in-ci.md for the
; audit that found this and the drift each file had accumulated as a result.
;
; Each rule below runs one file's `describe`/`test` blocks through the real
; `march test` runner, judged by exit code, so a regression here fails
; `dune runtest` instead of waiting for someone to remember to run the file
; by hand.
;
; Two of the 37 are deliberately NOT included:
;   - test_island_bridges.march: 7 of its tests fail due to a genuine,
;     tracked compiler bug (derive Json's `from_json` dispatch is broken
;     for the auto-generated island-bridge feature in BOTH the interpreted
;     and compiled paths -- not test-file drift). See
;     specs/todos/2026-08-12-island-bridge-from-json-broken.md.
;   - test_properties.march: passes, but its 76 Check.all property runs are
;     extremely slow under the tree-walking interpreter; wired separately
;     below under its own alias so it does not block the default `runtest`.

(rule
 (alias runtest)
 (deps %{exe:../bin/main.exe} (source_tree ../stdlib) (file stdlib/test_actor.march))
