; ── test_properties.march: wired separately, own alias ───────────────────
; Passes (228/228), but its 76 Check.all property runs (100 samples each,
; generating/round-tripping nested Msgpack/JSON values through the
; tree-walking interpreter) are genuinely slow -- a full run took several
; hours on a machine with ~8 other concurrent compiler sessions contending
; for CPU, and its true (uncontended) runtime hasn't been measured cleanly.
; Rather than guess and risk turning `dune runtest` into a multi-hour gate
; for every PR, this stays on its own alias, run explicitly:
;   dune build --root . @test/stdlib-march-properties
; A follow-up should benchmark it uncontended and, if it's actually fast,
; fold it into the main runtest block above alongside the other 35 files.
(rule
 (alias stdlib-march-properties)
 (deps %{exe:../bin/main.exe} (source_tree ../stdlib) (file stdlib/test_properties.march))
 (action (run %{exe:../bin/main.exe} test stdlib/test_properties.march)))
